The bridge is deployed with the AgentCore CLI, which scaffolds its own Python
project and resolves these packages (and their transitive dependencies) when
you build the runtime. a2a-bridge/requirements.txt and a2a-bridge/Dockerfile
are provided for reference.

Container base image (app/Dockerfile; a2a-bridge/Dockerfile for reference)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
python:3.12-slim (pulled from public.ecr.aws/docker/library/python)
  Python interpreter: PSF License
  Debian base OS packages: various (predominantly GPL, LGPL, and permissive
    licenses per Debian)

No additional OS packages are installed on top of the base image.

Note: no prebuilt container image is distributed in this repository. Consumers
build the image themselves from the Dockerfile, at which point the licenses
above apply to their locally built artifact.
